@startuml
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2E7D32
skinparam sequenceActorBackgroundColor #FFF3E0
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #E65100
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #757575
title **Secuencia: Patrones Comunicación Microservicios (Sync gRPC + Async Kafka + Shared Redis)**
actor "Clinical Service\n(Expediente Médico)" as Clinical
participant "API Gateway\n(mTLS)" as Gateway
participant "Auth Service\n(gRPC + REST)" as Auth
participant "Redis Cluster\n(Shared)" as Redis
participant "PostgreSQL\n(Shared + Own)" as DB
participant "Kafka\n(Message Broker)" as Kafka
participant "Audit Service\n(Own DB + ES)" as Audit
participant "Governance Service\n(Compliance)" as Governance
group **1. Validación Token Síncrona (gRPC - Clinical → Auth)**
    Clinical -> Gateway : GET /api/expedientes/123\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\nX-Tenant-ID: tenant-001
    Gateway -> Gateway : TLS 1.3 + mTLS\nRate limit + WAF
    Gateway -> Auth : gRPC ValidateToken\n{access_token, tenant_id, required_permission}
    Auth -> Auth : Validate JWT signature (JWKS local cache)\nCheck exp, nbf, iss, aud
    Auth -> Redis : EXISTS blocklist:{jti} (O(1))
    alt Token en blocklist
        Auth --> Clinical : gRPC Response: valid=false, error="Token Revoked"
        Clinical --> Gateway : 401 Token Revoked
    else Token válido
        Auth -> Auth : Extract claims + Check permission\n(roles, tenant_id match, scope)
        Auth --> Clinical : gRPC Response: valid=true\n{user_id, roles, tenant_id, session_id, device_id, expires_at, jwks_keys}
        Clinical -> Clinical : Cache validation result (TTL 30s)\nLocal JWKS para validación offline
        Clinical -> DB : SELECT with RLS (tenant_id)
        Clinical --> Gateway : 200 OK {expediente...}
        Gateway --> Clinical : 200 OK
    end
end
group **2. Evento Asíncrono: UserLoggedIn (Auth → Kafka → Consumers)**
    Auth -> Auth : Login successful (UserLoggedIn Domain Event)
    Auth -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.auth.user_logged_in\nKey: user_id\nHeaders: trace_id, span_id, timestamp
    par **Consumer: Governance Service**
        Kafka -> Governance : CONSUME UserLoggedInEvent
        Governance -> Governance : Enrich + Store audit trail\nCheck anomalies (geo, device, time)
        Governance -> Governance : Alert if suspicious (impossible travel, new device)
        and **Consumer: Audit Service**
        Kafka -> Audit : CONSUME UserLoggedInEvent
        Audit -> Audit : Persist to audit_log (own DB)\nIndex in Elasticsearch (user_id, tenant_id, timestamp)
        and **Consumer: Clinical Service (Cache Invalidation)**
        Kafka -> Clinical : CONSUME UserLoggedInEvent
        Clinical -> Clinical : Invalidate user session cache\nUpdate "last_login" in user profile
    end
    note right of Kafka
        **Kafka Topics:**
        - tenants.auth.user_created (6 partitions, 7d)
        - tenants.auth.user_logged_in (12 partitions, 3d)
        - tenants.auth.session_revoked (6 partitions, 7d)
        - tenants.auth.mfa_challenged (3 partitions, 3d)
        - tenants.auth.refresh_reuse_detected (3 partitions, 30d)
        - tenants.auth.account_locked (3 partitions, 7d)
        **Config:**
        - acks=all, min.insync.replicas=2
        - exactly-once semantics (transactions)
        - Retention: 3-30d por topic
    end note
end
group **3. Revocación Distribuida: Force-Revoke Admin**
    actor "Admin Tenant" as Admin
    Admin -> Gateway : DELETE /admin/users/{userId}/sessions
    Gateway -> Auth : gRPC ForceRevokeSessions\n{user_id, reason: force_revoke, requester_id
}
Auth -> Redis : KEYS refresh:{
    user_id
}
:* (TODAS las sesiones)
loop Por cada refresh token
    Auth -> Redis : GET key → {jti_access}
    Auth -> Redis : SET blocklist:{jti_access} TTL=exp-now
    Auth -> Redis : DEL refresh key
end
Auth -> Redis : KEYS session:{
    user_id
}
:* → DEL todas
Auth -> DB : INSERT audit_log (REVOKE_SESSION, force_revoke)
Auth -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.auth.session_revoked\n{user_id, tenant_id, reason: force_revoke, revoked_count, requester_id}
par **Notificación Inmediata (gRPC Stream / WebSocket)**
    Auth --> Gateway : Server-Sent Events / WebSocket\n{type: session_revoked, user_id, reason}
    Gateway --> Admin : Real-time notification
    and **Consumers Async (Kafka)**
    Kafka -> Clinical : CONSUME SessionRevokedEvent
    Clinical -> Clinical : Invalidate user cache\nReject pending requests for user
    Kafka -> Governance : CONSUME SessionRevokedEvent
    Governance -> Governance : Log compliance event\nNotify security team if force_revoke
    Kafka -> Audit : CONSUME SessionRevokedEvent
    Audit -> Audit : Persist + Index in ES
end
Auth --> Gateway : gRPC Response: {
    revoked_sessions: N}
    Gateway --> Admin : 200 OK
end
group **4. JWKS Rotation + Cache Invalidation (Cada 24h)**
    participant "Key Management\n(Vault/HSM)" as Vault
    Vault -> Vault : Rotate RSA keys (cada 24h)\nGenerate new key pair (kid: key-2)
    Vault -> Auth : Push new private key\nUpdate JWKS endpoint
    Auth -> Auth : Update in-memory JWKS cache\nSign new tokens with key-2\nAccept tokens signed with key-1 (overlap 1h)
    Auth -> Redis : PUBLISH jwks_rotated\n{new_kid: key-2, rotated_at: timestamp}
    par **Consumers: API Gateway + Clinical + Governance**
        Redis -> Gateway : SUBSCRIBE jwks_rotated
        Gateway -> Gateway : Fetch new JWKS from Auth\nUpdate local cache (TTL 1h)
        Redis -> Clinical : SUBSCRIBE jwks_rotated
        Clinical -> Clinical : Fetch new JWKS\nUpdate local validation cache
        Redis -> Governance : SUBSCRIBE jwks_rotated
        Governance -> Governance : Update validation keys
    end
    note right of Vault
        **Key Rotation Strategy:**
        - Rotación cada 24h (configurable)
        - Overlap: 1h aceptando key anterior
        - JWKS endpoint: /.well-known/jwks.json
        - Cache TTL: 1h en consumers
        - Claves en HashiCorp Vault / AWS KMS / Azure Key Vault
    end note
end
group **5. CDC: Cambios en Membresías (Debezium → Kafka → Consumers)**
    actor "Admin Tenant" as Admin
    Admin -> Gateway : PATCH /admin/users/{id} {roles: [MEDICO, AUDITOR]
}
Gateway -> Auth : PATCH /admin/users/{
    id}
    Auth -> DB : UPDATE hospital_memberships\nSET role_code = 'AUDITOR', updated_at = NOW()\nWHERE user_id = ? AND hospital_id = ?
    Auth -> DB : INSERT audit_log (USER_ROLE_CHANGED)
    par **Debezium CDC (PostgreSQL → Kafka)**
        DB -> Debezium : Capture WAL changes\n(hospital_memberships UPDATE)
        Debezium -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.db.hospital_memberships\n{op: "u", before: {...}, after: {...}, ts_ms}
    end
    par **Consumers: Clinical + Governance + Auth (cache invalidation)**
        Kafka -> Clinical : CONSUME membership_changed
        Clinical -> Clinical : Invalidate user permission cache\nNext request fetches fresh roles
        Kafka -> Governance : CONSUME membership_changed
        Governance -> Governance : Update compliance records\nRe-evaluate access grants
        Kafka -> Auth : CONSUME membership_changed
        Auth -> Auth : Invalidate user roles cache\nNext login fetches fresh roles
    end
    note right of Debezium
        **Debezium CDC Config:**
        - Connector: PostgreSQL Source
        - Tables: central_users, hospital_memberships, hospitals
        - Transform: ExtractNewRecordState
        - Topic prefix: tenants.db.
        - Schema registry: Avro + Schema Registry
    end note
end
group **6. Saga: Alta Usuario Cross-Module (Patrón Futuro)**
    note right of Auth
        **Saga Orchestrator (Auth Service):**
        1. Create User (central_users + memberships)
        2. Create Clinical Profile (async → Clinical)
        3. Create Audit Profile (async → Audit)
        4. Send Activation Email (async → Email)
        Compensación: Rollback en orden inverso si falla paso 2-4
    end note
    Admin -> Gateway : POST /admin/users {email, name, roles}
    Gateway -> Auth : Create User (Saga Inicio)
    Auth -> DB : INSERT central_users + hospital_memberships
    Auth -> DB : INSERT audit_log (USER_CREATED)
    Auth -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.saga.user_created\n{user_id, tenant_id, roles, saga_id, step: 1}
    par **Paso 2: Clinical Profile (Async)**
        Kafka -> Clinical : CONSUME saga.user_created (step 1)
        Clinical -> Clinical : Create patient profile / user preferences
        Clinical -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.saga.clinical_profile_created\n{saga_id, step: 2, success: true}
        and **Paso 3: Audit Profile (Async)**
        Kafka -> Audit : CONSUME saga.user_created (step 1)
        Audit -> Audit : Initialize audit trail for user
        Audit -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.saga.audit_profile_created\n{saga_id, step: 3, success: true}
    end
    par **Saga Orchestrator (Auth) - Coordinación**
        Auth -> Auth : Wait for steps 2, 3 (timeout 30s)
        alt Todos success
            Auth -> DB : UPDATE user SET saga_status = 'COMPLETED'
            Auth -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.saga.completed {saga_id}
            Auth -> Email : Send activation email
        else Algún fallo / Timeout
            Auth -> Auth : COMPENSACIÓN
            Auth -> Kafka : PRODUCE tenants.saga.compensate {saga_id, failed_step}
            Clinical -> Clinical : DELETE profile (compensación)
            Audit -> Audit : DELETE audit init (compensación)
            Auth -> DB : DELETE user + memberships (compensación)
        end
    end
end
box "Resumen Patrones" #E8F5E9
note as N1
**SYNC (gRPC):**
- ValidateToken (Clinical → Auth)
- ForceRevokeSessions (Admin → Auth)
- Latencia objetivo: < 5ms p99
- Circuit Breaker + Retry (3x, exp backoff)
**ASYNC (Kafka):**
- Domain Events (UserLoggedIn, SessionRevoked, etc.)
- CDC (Debezium) para cambios BD
- Saga Orchestration (futuro)
- Exactly-once semantics
**SHARED INFRASTRUCTURE:**
- Redis Cluster: Blocklist, Sessions, Rate Limits
- PostgreSQL: Shared tables (central_users) + Own tables
- JWKS Rotation: Redis Pub/Sub para invalidación cache
end note
end box
@enduml
